e,"_score_shrhldr_yield":85.8,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.038510002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":25.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Sabine Royalty Trust holds royalty and mineral interests in various producing oil and gas properties in the United States. The company's royalty and mineral interests include landowner's royalties, overriding royalty interests, minerals, production payments, and other similar non-participatory interests in certain producing and proved undeveloped oil and gas properties located in Florida, Louisiana, Mississippi, New Mexico, Oklahoma, and Texas. Sabine Royalty Trust was incorporated in 1982 and is based in Dallas, Texas.","financial_summary":["Sabine Royalty Trust is a small-cap energy business with a $937M market cap on $77M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -15% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 8.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average SGA growth (16% YoY) warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 79% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 32% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (SBR)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_SBR_111326111401_1794586441.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sabine Royalty Trust declares $0.36039 dividend (SBR:NYSE)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668787-sabine-royalty-trust-declares-0_36039-dividend","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794237924.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765